            </note>
            <note corresp="#d325-f3" n="59" xml:id="d325-f3-content">
                <p>John S. Hooker, Assistant Executive Secretary of the Board of Economic
                    Operations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d325-f4" n="60" xml:id="d325-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d325-f5" n="61" xml:id="d325-f5-content">
                <p>Carlos Mendieta was President of Cuba, 1934–35.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d325-f6" n="62" xml:id="d325-f6-content">
                <p>No definite action was taken during 1942 with regard to this proposed
                    Export-Import Bank loan for the Habana waterworks project. A source of delay was
                    the choice of a consulting engineer by the Bank.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
